{"type":"standard","title":"Demta language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Demta language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q14466283","titles":{"canonical":"Demta_language","normalized":"Demta language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Demta language</span></span>"},"pageid":31503886,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1322819389","tid":"33c6067e-c423-11f0-b3a3-b231b5d4925a","timestamp":"2025-11-18T02:06:32Z","description":"Papuan language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demta_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demta_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demta_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Demta_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demta_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Demta_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demta_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Demta_language"}},"extract":"Demta, also known as Sowari and Muris, is a Papuan language spoken by the Demta people on the north coast of Papua, Indonesia. It is spoken in Ambora, Muris Besar, Muris Kecil, and Yougafsa villages, all located in Demta District.","extract_html":"<p><b>Demta</b>, also known as <b>Sowari</b> and <b>Muris</b>, is a Papuan language spoken by the Demta people on the north coast of Papua, Indonesia. It is spoken in <span class=\"extiw\">Ambora</span>, Muris Besar, <span class=\"extiw\">Muris Kecil</span>, and <span class=\"extiw\">Yougafsa</span> villages, all located in <span class=\"extiw\">Demta District</span>.</p>"}